FINAL ANSWER:
Max Bruckner wrote most of the code that's still in `cJSON.c` and `cJSON.h`: 75.1% of the surviving lines.

The tool is `surviving-lines`, which counts lines with `git blame -w -M -C` at HEAD. It attributed 3,596 of 3,601 lines across the two files. I used `--merge-identities`, which merges same-person addresses in memory only and writes nothing.

